# Railway runs one process per service, so these are two services off this same repo rather
# than two processes of one. Both need the same environment variables.
#
#   web    — the API. One replica on purpose: flask-limiter's counters live in this process's
#            memory, so a second replica doubles every limit. Raising it means Redis first
#            (RATELIMIT_STORAGE_URI).
#   worker — drives tailoring runs. Separate so a deploy restarts the API without killing a
#            run in flight; a killed worker loses nothing, because its lease expires and the
#            next one resumes from the last step on disk.
web: gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:$PORT --workers 1 --threads 4 --timeout 120 app:app
worker: flask --app app tailoring-worker
